  "blocksOrielShowed": [
    "Computed by Oriel from the index and its change log: Counted by State, highest first",
    "Computed by Oriel from the index and its change log: Done, counted by week, running, since Sep 2. Least-squares line over 7 whole weeks, R² 0.94, 0.8 a week. At that rate the 9 left get there around Jan 14 (Dec 21 – Mar 16, 80%), if no more are added",
    "Computed by Oriel from the index and its change log, where Done is blank: State, Assignee, Estimate, Days in its state. ≥ marks a value that is only a lower bound: it began before the change log starts"
  ],
  "reply": "No, it's very unlikely. It's 29 October, so two days are left this month, and 9 of the 14 items in the checkout epic SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards are still open. Oriel's trend line (the second chart below) puts the finish around mid-January. Even its earliest likely date is late December.\n\n**Where things stand (charts below):**\n- **Done: 5.** That's 3 stories and 2 bugs.\n- **In progress: 4.** SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message has been in progress for 22 days and SYN-92 Show the fare breakdown before payment for 15. SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website and SYN-104 Handle 3-D Secure challenges in the native checkout started more recently.\n- **Not started: 5.** All of them have sat in To do for about 8 weeks, including SYN-10 Remove the legacy web-view checkout, SYN-57 Checkout analytics: drop-off by step, SYN-88 Refund to the original payment method when a sailing is cancelled and SYN-98 Apply promo codes at checkout.\n- **Pace:** the team has been finishing just under one item a week since early September.\n\n**Who has the open work:** Amara Okafor has three items, Chen Yuting and Dara Nikolaidis have two each, and Esme Whitlock and Greta Lindqvist have one each. Three open items have no estimate, so the remaining effort is hard to size.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- This workstream is empty, so I searched your other sources to find the epic. What I found there is read-only from here.\n- I didn't see the epic's target date or its description, so I can't say whether \"this month\" was the plan.\n\nIf it helps, I can add the epic and its items to this workstream so you can follow them here. Or I can help you decide what to cut to finish sooner."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
